<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Fill presets of our own, in the original editor's own format.

  The game ships nine presets in <game>/Editor/FillPresets.xml, all of them
  named "(test)" and most of them one layer deep. These are the woods and
  meadows a map actually wants, written the same way so either file can be
  edited by hand and either can be dropped beside the game.

  Read the fields in src/fill/preset.ts; the algorithm they drive is in
  src/fill/plan.ts and documented in docs/FILL_TOOL.md. The short version:

    Dispersion  grid spacing in tiles — smaller is denser
    Width       how much further from the painted edge the LATER layers start
    Probability chance one lattice point of this layer keeps its candidate
    Size        radius in tiles, kept clear of the edge and of other objects

  So a preset reads outward-in: grass at Width 0 covers the whole patch,
  undergrowth starts half a tile in, trees a further three quarters.
-->
