    <!--
      Cave Walls — the one preset here meant to be IMPASSABLE.

      Every other preset dresses ground a hero walks over; this one fills the
      rock a cave is cut through, and its pieces are the dungeon walls the game
      builds its own underground with: 3x3 blocks, so a run of them reads as a
      wall face rather than as boulders in a row. Probability 1 and a spacing
      just under their own width: gaps in a cave wall are holes in the world,
      not variety.

      The rubble layer is what keeps a straight edge from looking cut, and it is
      allowed to thin out.
    -->
    <Item>
      <Name>Cave Walls</Name>
      <Layers>
        <Item>
          <objects>
            <Item><Object><Type>AdvMapStaticShared</Type><ID>Subterra\Dungeonwalls\Dungeonwall01</ID></Object><Size>1.4</Size><Probability>1</Probability></Item>
            <Item><Object><Type>AdvMapStaticShared</Type><ID>Subterra\Dungeonwalls\Dungeonwall03</ID></Object><Size>1.4</Size><Probability>1</Probability></Item>
